<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1827" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀζηχής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
		(prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-διἁσ̓<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εχής</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>continuous</i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀζαχής,
				ἀζεχήσ̓</span>
			<i>unceasing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδύνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρυμαγδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.741
				</span></i>
			: neut. as Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀζ&lt;&gt;χὲς φαγέμενκαὶπιέμεν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.3
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄϊες] ἀ. μεμακυῖαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.435
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄζα</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀζαλέος</span>) <i>hard, seasoned</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορύνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.99
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span> v.l.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.25
			</span></i>.</div>
